, "content": "engenn5le09ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The First Conditional"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " You can use the first conditional to talk about actions and situations in the future."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are two parts to the sentence. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "One part is the <span class=\"strong\">condition.</span> The other part is the <span class=\"strong\">result</span> ."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Form:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">If</span> + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">Simple Present tense</span>  + <span class=\"italic\">subject</span> + <span class=\"italic\">will/may/might</span> <br> You use a comma after the condition in this form. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can change the two parts of the sentence so that the result comes first.  "}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">If you want to find out,</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">you'll have to come back tomorrow.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Result\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Condition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I might believe you </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">if you show me what's inside.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Quantifiers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Quantifier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more<br> less/fewer <br>no/none<br> any /not any<br>  some <br> a lot of/lots of<br>plenty of<br> enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount <br> a smaller number/amount<br>  0, nothing<br>  to ask about / say there is not<br>  a small number/amount<br>  a very large number/amount<br>  more than you need<br>  as much as you need\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Did you buy enough groceries?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't see any eggs in here."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I may buy more bread."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "veal"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the meat from a young cow "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I like eating veal more than chicken."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob09aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " These are words you use to talk about about food and drinks."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "marsala "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "cooked with a sweet strong wine "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I made you some veal marsala."}, {"type": "audio", "